213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The YBX3 series employs an optimized cooling-fin arrangement. As motors become more compact and thermal loading increases, improved heat dissipation is essential. The cooling system is designed for effective heat removal during operation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (The motor has two independent airflow paths: an internal circuit and an external circuit. Much of the generated heat is transferred through the stator core to the frame and removed by external cooling air. The remaining heat, primarily from rotor losses and stator winding-end losses, is carried to the frame by internal airflow. External air passes along the cooling fins from the non-drive end toward the drive end. The terminal box is positioned away from the main high-velocity cooling airflow to reduce direct air impact.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
