258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 126 0 R
/T (Bearings are available in rolling-bearing and sleeve-bearing configurations. Rolling bearings are generally used; sleeve bearings are selected when operating conditions, such as speed, load capacity or duty requirements, exceed the applicable limits. Standard-design H500-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\), H560-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\) and H630-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\) motors use sleeve bearings with forced lubrication; H500-2 may also be configured with self-lubricating sleeve bearings. Other motors use rolling bearings with continuous oil filling and draining arrangements.)
/E (Bearings are available in rolling-bearing and sleeve-bearing configurations. Rolling bearings are generally used; sleeve bearings are selected when operating conditions, such as speed, load capacity or duty requirements, exceed the applicable limits. Standard-design H500-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\), H560-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\) and H630-2 \(6 kV, 10 kV\) motors use sleeve bearings with forced lubrication; H500-2 may also be configured with self-lubricating sleeve bearings. Other motors use rolling bearings with continuous oil filling and draining arrangements.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (Rolling-bearing assemblies include the end shield, bearing housing, inner and outer covers, bearing, oil slinger, retaining ring, continuous oil supply and drainage devices, and bearing-temperature monitoring. Oil-cup lubrication uses lithium-based grease. V-type sealing rings prevent dust and water from entering the bearings, extending service life and lubrication intervals. The calculated bearing service life exceeds 100,000 hours.)
/E (Rolling-bearing assemblies include the end shield, bearing housing, inner and outer covers, bearing, oil slinger, retaining ring, continuous oil supply and drainage devices, and bearing-temperature monitoring. Oil-cup lubrication uses lithium-based grease. V-type sealing rings prevent dust and water from entering the bearings, extending service life and lubrication intervals. The calculated bearing service life exceeds 100,000 hours.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
