270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (The stator winding uses Class 155 \(F\) insulation. The winding ends are firmly secured and tied. During manufacturing, multiple inter-turn impulse voltage and power-frequency withstand-voltage tests are performed. The VPI \(vacuum pressure impregnation\) solvent-free process provides high electrical and mechanical strength, corrosion resistance and moisture resistance. Special anti-corona treatment of the winding core allows safe operation at higher altitudes.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Low-loss, high-efficiency silicon steel laminations are used for the punched core to reduce iron losses and improve efficiency and operating reliability. The optimized slot geometry and suitable magnetic slot wedges can reduce iron loss by an average of 20%, increase efficiency by over 0.3%, improve power factor and reduce stator temperature rise.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 127 0 R
