2281 0 obj
<<
/Title (An optimized rotor dynamic design, innovative manufacturing processes and high-precision dynamic balancing ensure low vibration levels. The YBX3 series high-efficiency high-voltage flameproof three-phase induction motors not only meet the vibration requirements of GB 10068, but also achieve levels substantially better than the standard in most applications.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2268 0 R
/First 2293 0 R
/Last 2293 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2294 0 R
>>
endobj
2282 0 obj
<<
/Title (2.5 Frame and End-Shield Structure)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2268 0 R
/Prev 2295 0 R
>>
endobj
2283 0 obj
<<
/Title (The motor frame and end shields are made of high-quality cast iron of grade HT250 or above, using established manufacturing processes. Each motor center height corresponds to a specific frame, with integral cast feet. The optimized frame design provides excellent strength and rigidity. The horizontally or vertically mounted cast-iron frame features full-length cooling ribs and four axial ventilation passages. Axial parallel cooling fins are arranged around the winding end regions inside the frame to increase heat-dissipation area. The terminal box can be mounted on either side of the motor. The drive-end and non-drive-end end shields have the same structure, with internal and external cooling ribs to improve rigidity and cooling performance \(Figure 5\).)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2268 0 R
/First 2296 0 R
/Last 2296 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2297 0 R
>>
endobj
